A||||14||Brandon86SE||URGENT!!!!  Tranny (I think) Problems!||||9||
Z||000000||Brandon86SE||10-12-2001||12:05 AM||||Ok, I have a 86SE with the 2.8 and 4-speed Isuzu.  It has 97,000km's on it.  A new clutch was put in 11 months ago.  This afternoon, leaving school, I got a squeal coming from the engine when I started the car up.  Then as I tried to go into first it squealed more, and then kinda grinded.  At first, it squealed whenever I was putting the clutch in, or shifting gears (first and second only, though....).  I took it on the freeway to get home, and once I got here it had stopped.  However, I knew I had to do something, now, because I'm supposed to be taking a road trip tomorrow.  I took it into a mr. lube to have 'em take a look at my tranny fluid, since I've never changed it, and I do have a slight leak in it.  They couldn't help, 'cause it isn't a dipstick tranny.  So I brought it to a mechanics shop, and paid $80 for a tranny fluid flush.  When I picked it up it seemed fine, and I took it to work and parked it.  I left work a couple hours later, and it was squealing again, not right after I started it up, but within 30s.  This time it didn't go away, so I shut off the car, and restarted it, it was quiet then, until I got home.  It started squealing with the clutch fully engaged when pulling into my driveway, as soon as I disengaged the clutch the noise was gone.  Now, I'm supposed to be heading on a 3hr roadtrip to visit a friend tomorrow, I need to know if something's seriously wrong, or if it takes a little bit for the gearlube to get around, and I just need to drive it a bit more, or what's up.  Please help quickly, thanks,<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Neal||10-12-2001||12:46 AM||||Hey Brandon, its not your accessory belt is it?  Or any of the attached parts water pump, alternator, or ac?<P>What kind of squeel are you talking about?<P>hell if your in my part of town tomorrow ill look at it for ya, to get a second oppinion and all.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Brandon86SE||10-12-2001||12:54 AM||||Neal - I'm SE, in Diamond Bay.  I just replaced the belt 2 weeks ago, 'cause I had heard a squeal a couple times before, and figured that was it.  This only seems to be going when the clutch is engaged.  I'm kinda thinking it might be the release bearing on the clutch, but maybe the belt is slipping, but that probably would've happened before now if it were installed wrong.<P>Brandon||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rick 88||10-12-2001||12:55 AM||||Brandon,<P>It may be your throwout bearing has gone bad.<BR>What kind did you install when you replaced the clutch?<P>Rick 88||||reg||1
Z||000004||Neal||10-12-2001||01:17 AM||||Rick may have nailed it<P>but new belts do go bad sometimes, also when the clutch is engaged a slightly different load is on the engine that can cause a just barely right belt to slip<P>but ill be at the university from about 930 till 4, err ill leave home and get home at those times... ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Brandon86SE||10-12-2001||01:27 AM||||well, I'm talking to a mechanic on ICQ right now, and he seems to thin that the freeplay was set too tight by the guys who did my clutch a year aog.  This would cause the throw-out bearing to not fully disengage from the diaphram, and wear really, really fast.  They gave me 1yr, 20,000km warranty on the job.  It's been 11 months, and just over 20,000km's, I think I'm gonna raise hell about how they f***ed up my car, and better damn well fix it!  Problem being, they're in Medicine Hat, 3 hours away.  GRR!!!!!!!!||||reg||8
Z||000006||Jefrysuko||10-12-2001||01:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Brandon86SE:<BR><B>well, I'm talking to a mechanic on ICQ right now, and he seems to thin that the freeplay was set too tight by the guys who did my clutch a year aog.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You can't adjust that on our cars.  Nice try though.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Jefrysuko||10-12-2001||01:37 AM||||Have you thought of the possibility that the belt you had installed recently has stretched and needs to be retightened.  I always have to do that shortly after putting on a new belt.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Brandon86SE||10-12-2001||01:40 AM||||I've checked the belt, it's tight.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Pike||10-12-2001||01:49 AM||||He dude...In order to determine throw-out bearing, start the engine and keep it in neutral. Now get your head down there right next to the clutch pedal. now very slowly begin to engage the clutch. If the throw-out bearing is bad, you will hear/feel it in a very pronounced manner through the pedal as you engage the clutch...then get those bastards to fix it again for free! Offer to split the cost if they won't move on it.<BR>Pike||||reg||1
Z||000010||Brandon86SE||10-12-2001||02:08 AM||||Pike, I just did what you said, and there was no squeal there.  I started the car, and tried immediately with my hand on the clutch and head right there.  Nothing then, I then let it run for 30s or so, and tried a couple more times, still nothing.  I dunno if this is still just an occasional thing though, maybe I had a bad day, and won't hear anything tomorrow.  But still we figure that's the problem, eh?  If so, I'm still gonna call the guys who did my clutch tomorrow and raise hell.<P>Brandon||||reg||1
Z||000011||stsmithgt||10-12-2001||07:38 PM||||Is the squeal a belt squeal or a metalic sqeal like metal on metal?  Mine squealed bad when my clutch fork gave out and jammed up the throw out bearing into the pressure plate. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> That was an ugly noise especially at 10:00 p.m..  Sometimes the old parts matched up with new parts can't handle it.  It's a weird looking fork so if your not familiar with them, it can be overlooked as worn out.  I don't think a belt would be making noise because of pushing in your clutch.  If your car was idling and you heard the squeal just by pushing in the clutch, I would lean towards the problem being related to the throw out bearing if not the bearing itself.  The demand on the belts hadn't changed so they wouldn't have a reason at that time to start squealing.<BR>  Another theory for the noise stopping could be that the fork or bearing  was out of position binding up to make the squealing noise, but then settled back into place enough to eliminate the noise.  I expect at least the noise will come back and at the most unopportune moment like in the middle of a road trip.  I don't mean to be so negative, but this happen to me.  I was only 300 miles away from home, but only 5 miles away from the mechanic I use. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>If you're going to chew them out over  their work, Keep a cool head.  You'll get further.  I don't think I could after all that I saw wrong on mine so I didn't go back YET.  Can't think straight when I'm mad. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||roadwarrior||10-12-2001||11:04 PM||||did you change your reelease bearing when you did the clutch? if not, that is more than likely your problem||||reg||1
Z||000013||Brandon86SE||10-15-2001||01:41 AM||||Alright guys, me and a friend came back to my house after school on Friday and took a listen/ look at the car.  He figured it was my AC belt, so we ripped it off and had a look, it was totally shot!  We picked up a new one, but couldn't get it on.  I'm gonna have to go to a shop and get 'em to put it on.  Anyway, I went to Edmonton and back this weekend and the car seemed to run alright.  However, on Friday night, I stil got a bit of a squeal for a bit, and then again tonight...  The squeal is probably the alt. belt, 'cause we also took that off and back on, maybe needs to be tightened again....?  But what bugs me is the grinding sound I hear when going into first still.....  any suggestions?<P>Brandon||||reg||1
Z||000014||Pike||10-15-2001||01:52 AM||||Well...if the squeel was belt related, then the grind into first could be a bad synchro inside the trans. I had one that did that for 4 years and I finally sold the car to a friend and it did it for another 2 years then suddenly quit making the grind one day! Who knew!<BR>Pike||||reg||1
